From 0e70f50cc7175c1de2a56b06f35be9f0872e749f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sophia Wen <h_f_wen@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 11:50:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add 2Q-aware changed-flag loop exit for Level 2
 optimization
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace FixedPoint(size) + FixedPoint(depth) convergence check with a
direct changed-flag from Rust optimization passes. Only multi-qubit gate
changes (RemoveIdentityEquivalent, CommutativeCancellation) trigger
re-iteration — 1Q-only changes do not, since they cannot create new 2Q
optimization opportunities.

Result: 5/6 test circuits exit after 1 iteration (was 2-3 with
FixedPoint), zero 2Q gate regressions. Level 1 and Level 3 are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
